    <string name="setup_oem_body_oppo">OPPO / ColorOS restricts background apps. Tap below to open Startup manager, then allow Notix to start automatically.</string>
    <string name="setup_oem_body_oneplus">OnePlus restricts background activity by default. Tap below to allow Notix to launch in the background.</string>
    <string name="setup_oem_body_vivo">Vivo restricts background apps. Tap below to open Background startup management, then allow Notix.</string>
    <string name="setup_oem_body_samsung">Samsung\'s Device Care can put Notix to sleep. Tap below to open Battery settings, then mark Notix as Unrestricted (Battery → Background usage limits).</string>
    <string name="setup_oem_body_asus">ASUS Mobile Manager restricts background apps. Tap below to open Auto-start manager and enable Notix.</string>
    <string name="setup_oem_body_letv">Letv restricts background apps. Tap below to open Autoboot management.</string>
    <string name="setup_oem_body_meizu">Meizu restricts background apps. Tap below to open Security settings.</string>
    <string name="setup_oem_body_nokia">Nokia uses an Evenwell power-saving layer that can kill Notix. Tap below to add it to the protected list.</string>
